  "notes": "Gospel-belt hip-hop soul out of the Bad Boy / Def Soul orbit, 1998–2003. The research calls the ballad spine \"**48–66 half-time** — the slowest documented band here alongside H-Town\", with seven sourced tempos inside it, so 48–66 felt is the base with `halfTime` true; the single 98 uptempo is a boom-bap 2&4 and is a different backbeat class. Three drum deltas: \"at 48–62 the kit is a single kick per bar\" (one hit, syncopation 0.03), \"plus a snare on 3\", and \"a live-feel tambourine\" — a downbeat tambourine and snap bed at two to four hits a bar with `quantizeStrength` dropped to 0.6, which is what \"live-feel\" means on this schema; the hat lane falls to an 8th base at 0.04. The identifying parameter is harmonic: \"full gospel harmonic vocabulary — passing diminished chords, ii–V–I… choir-stack backgrounds\". `ii–v–i` takes top weight, a `vii°` passing family is authored (the numeral parser reads the degree and the dim marker; the quality lives in `extensions`), and `susOrDimProb` is raised. \"Very high note-density in the ad-lib runs\" is the 4–12 density, the widest in this section, with the highest arch weight and a real octave-jump rate. The low end is \"organ pedal and sustained bass on the root; the low end is church-organ-derived rather than 808\" — so no `bass808` block. ⚠ The research marks the tritone-substitution claim and the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`; the tritone substitution has no schema field and is recorded here rather than encoded. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode with gospel modulations [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
